 "descriptions": [
  {
   "descriptionType": "Abstract",
   "description": "<p>Led by Tahiti&#x2019;s biomedical research center, Institute Louis Malard&#xE9; (ILM) and the UC Gump South Pacific Research Station on Moorea, the MOZEROA (<italic>mo-zie-roh-ah)</italic> project draws on successful trials on Tetiaroa atoll to target Huahine for the first island-wide mosquito elimination on a high island. <italic>MOZEROA 2030: Innovative Mosquito Control on Huahine Island (</italic>the Project) aims to suppress and eventually eliminate the risk of mosquito-borne diseases (&#x201C;mosquito net zero&#x201D;) from Huahine as proof of concept for treating entire islands in French Polynesia by 2030.</p>"
